I checked the current official docs. Claude Code is described as an agentic coding tool that reads the codebase, edits files, runs commands, and works across multiple files/tools, so I would use it for deep audits, architecture planning, accessibility reasoning, and large multi-file refactors. ([Claude Platform Docs][1]) Codex is described as OpenAI’s coding agent that can read, edit, and run code, and Codex cloud can work on background/parallel tasks in its own cloud environment, so I would use it for clear implementation batches, fixes, token sweeps, tests, and verification. ([OpenAI Platform][2])

